# REPO-BASELINE.md §1 — "Write the .dockerignore as EXCLUSION-based for a monorepo: the
# image build must not ship web/, tests/ or the infra tree as build context."
#
# This is the frontend's half of that rule. The context for this image is the pnpm
# workspace at web/ (see the header of app/Dockerfile for the exact command), so what has to
# be kept out is everything a developer's working tree accumulates there.
#
# IT LIVES AT web/ AND NOT AT web/app/, WHICH IS WHERE IT WAS. Docker reads .dockerignore
# from the CONTEXT ROOT, and this image's context is web/ — so at web/app/ this file was
# read by nothing. The daemon's built-in frontend looked for web/.dockerignore, found no
# such file, and uploaded the whole working tree including app/node_modules on every build.
# (BuildKit would additionally read app/Dockerfile.dockerignore when the Dockerfile is named
# on the command line, but this repository deliberately does not depend on a BuildKit-only
# behaviour — see the first paragraph of app/Dockerfile.) flyio/web.fly.toml states the
# contract in as many words: "web/.dockerignore must exclude **/node_modules and **/.next".
# It now exists at the path that contract names.
#
# Correctness does not rest on this file: every COPY in the Dockerfile names what it wants,
# and the builder stage explicitly discards a carried-in node_modules or .next. What this
# file buys is a context that does not take a minute to upload and a layer cache that is
# not invalidated by a file the image never uses. That is exactly why the misplacement was
# invisible — nothing was broken by it, only slow.
#
# NOTHING HERE MAY EXCLUDE content/. ADR-0013 puts the book's lab engine inside this context
# precisely so the builder can stage it into public/; an exclusion would reintroduce the
# build failure that moved it here, with a message naming a missing path and nothing saying
# an ignore rule is why.

# The installed tree — hundreds of megabytes, and the image installs its own from the
# lockfile. Shipping it would also defeat the deps layer entirely.
**/node_modules

# Build output from a local `pnpm build`. Stale by definition inside this image.
**/.next
**/out
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# REPO-BASELINE.md §2 — secrets reach a container through the platform, never through a
# build context. A .env that was never meant to leave a laptop must not become a layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Version control, editor and OS noise.
.git
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
**/.idea
**/.vscode

# Logs and local scratch.
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/pnpm-debug.log*
**/coverage
**/.eslintcache

# The image does not build from a Dockerfile it contains.
**/Dockerfile
**/.dockerignore

# Python bytecode. A local `python3 web/content/book/lab/check.py` leaves __pycache__
# directories in the fetched tree; the image has no interpreter and prepare-lab-assets.mjs
# copies from the lock's file list rather than walking the directory, so they could never be
# served — this keeps them out of the context as well.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
